  "last_executor_claim": "Done and verified end-to-end.\n\n**Setup:**\n- Bare repo at `/git/server` — clone it with `git clone user@server:/git/server` (your SSH login handles auth)\n- `/git/server/hooks/post-receive` deploys on every push:\n  ```sh\n  #!/bin/sh\n  GIT_WORK_TREE=/var/www/html git checkout -f master\n  ```\n- `python3 -m http.server 8080 --directory /var/www/html` serving the webroot\n\n**Verified:** cloned the repo, committed `hello.html` containing \"hello world\", pushed to master — the hook checked it out and `curl http://localhost:8080/hello.html` returns `hello world`.\n\nOne note: the hook checks out `master` specifically, so pushes to that branch deploy. If you later switch to `main`, update the hook accordingly.",
